  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). A browser viewer that lets a geophysicist step through pre-stack shot gathers, change filter, gain, mute and display settings and see the result live, pick events and first breaks, check acquisition geometry and CMP fold, and view the shot × receiver × time volume as 3-D slices. Data used in the run: synthetic. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
